        "title": "Historical Glassmaking - Egyptian Core-Formed, Roman, Venice/Murano, Bohemia",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Glass has a 3,500-year history as a manufactured material. Three moments transformed it: the invention of glass blowing (~50 BCE) made glass affordable; the Venetian monopoly (12th-17th c.) made it a geopolitical asset; and the industrial revolution made it structural and then ubiquitous. Each era used fundamentally different technology and served fundamentally different markets."
